<h2>Using this website</h2>
<p>This website is built to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. You should be able to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>zoom in up to 400% without the text spilling off the screen</li>
  <li>change colours, contrast levels and fonts using your browser or device settings</li>
  <li>navigate the whole website using just a keyboard or speech recognition software</li>
  <li>listen to the website using a screen reader</li>
  <li>stop the photo slideshow on the home page using the pause button</li>
  <li>use the website with animations reduced, if you've turned on "reduce motion" on your device</li>
  <li>translate any page using the translate menu at the top of the page</li>
</ul>
<p>Body text is set at a large size with generous line spacing, and all text and buttons meet WCAG AA colour contrast.</p>

<h2>Known issues</h2>
<p>Translations come from Google Translate and may contain mistakes. Photographs on the website are described in text for people who can't see them.</p>

<h2>Information in other formats</h2>
